findings=[
 ('TMZ342-01','Missing pre-dose hold thresholds','Original assessment reduced only at ANC<1.0 or platelets<50, leaving the current ANC1.0–<1.5 and platelet50–<100 range without a relevant restriction.','Current pre-dose thresholds ANC<1.5 and platelets<100 now withhold, explicitly attributed to EMA SmPC p7; independent NCCP nadir reductions retained.','EMA p7; NCCP p2 Table2'),
 ('TMZ342-02','Current counts and prior nadirs conflated','The original low-count rules immediately reduced one level without timing or previous-cycle context.','Separate current pre-dose fields and prior-cycle nadirs; recovery does not erase a nadir-triggered next-cycle reduction.','NCCP p2 Table2; EMA p7'),
 ('TMZ342-03','No episode, recovery or prior-dose safeguards','A one-level reduction could be shown with no previous dose or recovery context and no protection from repeating it.','Document prior100/150/200, recovery and episode action; review absent context; fresh reduction at100 has a stop pathway; an already-applied episode is not reduced twice.','NCCP p2 Tables1–2'),
 ('TMZ342-04','Starting-dose and escalation inputs did not drive a decision','Previously treated/naive status and dose level were recorded as context only.','Starting-dose reference separates naive200 from previously treated150; cycle2 increase is a guarded consultant decision; known conflicting nadirs suppress its criterion. No automatic numerical increase.','NCCP p1'),
 ('TMZ342-05','Recurrent duration ambiguity not surfaced','Table1 lists cycles2–6 although treatment paragraph continues until progression or unacceptable toxicity.','An explicit source conflict preserves open-ended recurrent schedule and flags beyond-cycle6 review; no automatic six-cycle cap.','NCCP p1 vs p2 Table1'),
 ('TMZ342-06','Hepatic exclusion missing','Original Child-Pugh A/B andC shared permissive caution output; significant hepatic dysfunction exclusion was not assessed.','Significant dysfunction exclusion and Child-PughC conflict review added; A/B remains separate; no invented ALT/bilirubin cutoff.','NCCP p1 exclusion vs p3 Table3; EMA pp5–6'),
 ('TMZ342-07','Dacarbazine allergy and severe myelosuppression missing','Generic component hypersensitivity did not explicitly represent dacarbazine; no severe-myelosuppression exclusion flag.','Separate source-backed exclusions added.','NCCP p1; EMA p6'),
 ('TMZ342-08','HBV positive screening pathway missing','Missing-screen and active-reactivation rules existed, but a positive serology before treatment did not trigger liver-specialist review.','Positive-serology review added alongside existing screening/reactivation gates.','NCCP pp2–3; EMA p6'),
 ('TMZ342-09','Important SmPC monitoring supplements absent','Original assessment did not explain day22 CBC or post-cycle LFT requirements.','Source-labelled Day22±48h CBC, weekly until recovery and after-each-cycle LFTs added; baseline glucose/HBV and day1 FBC/renal/LFT retained; no fixed MRI timing invented.','NCCP p2; EMA pp6–7'),
 ('TMZ342-10','Recovery inequality ambiguity','EMA minimum pre-dose criteria are inclusive, while weekly recovery monitoring uses strict greater-than values.','At exact1.5/100 after a previous reduction-triggering episode, review gate prevents automatic restart interpretation.','EMA p7, visually checked original PDF'),
 ('TMZ342-11','PJP and interaction risk absent','Recurrent monotherapy lacked explicit PJP/steroid and interaction-review pathways.','Risk-based PJP review distinct from mandatory42-day concurrent-RT prophylaxis; valproate and marrow-suppressive drug review added. Acute-infection hold gates are clearly marked clinical safety interpretations.','EMA pp6–8'),
 ('TMZ342-12','Incorrect CTCAE grade4 nausea/vomiting choices','Original v5 input options offered grade4 nausea and vomiting with fabricated generic grade4 descriptions.','Both inputs now stop at grade3; severe symptoms prompt review but do not incorrectly trigger the generic non-haematological discontinuation table, which excludes nausea/vomiting.','NCCP p2 exclusion; existing CTCAE v5 standard and EMA p7'),
 ('TMZ342-13','Male contraception sources differ','NCCP says six months after last dose; current EMA says at least three.','Both source positions documented; Irish six-month advice retained for team confirmation.','NCCP p3 vs EMA pp7,9')]
report=dict(release='0.84.38',code='00342',protocol_path=str(P.relative_to(R)),baseline_sha256=sha(O/'protocol-before/00342.json'),final_sha256=sha(P),source_documents=sources,source_version_change=False,old_rules=len(b['rule_engine']['rules']),new_rules=len(p['rule_engine']['rules']),old_inputs=len(b['input_definitions']),new_inputs=len(p['input_definitions']),source_checks=dict(total=cases['total'],passed=cases['passed'],failed=cases['failed'],rules_with_executed_positive_witnesses=len(json.loads((O/'criterion-matrix.json').read_text())),before_failed_expectations=prior['failed'],before_total=prior['total'],interpretation='Before failures include added-domain and structural expectations; they are not a count of distinct clinical defects.'),findings=[dict(id=id,title=t,before=old,after=new,source=s) for id,t,old,new,s in findings],source_conflicts=p['clinical_governance']['source_conflicts'],limitations=['Independent consultant oncology and pharmacy review pending; clinical use not authorised.','Browser/consent/patient/PDF integration belongs to the parent release validation and is not claimed by this isolated audit.','No patient-specific calculated dose is provided; even a fully specified reduction is an explicit consultant/pharmacy confirmation pathway.','No undocumented fixed MRI or tumour-marker schedule, six-cycle cap or universal PJP prophylaxis for the five-day recurrent regimen has been invented.'],migration=dict(removed_legacy_rule_ids=[x['id'] for x in b['rule_engine']['rules'] if x['id'] not in {y['id'] for y in p['rule_engine']['rules']}],removed_OF590_ids=[x['id'] for x in b['rule_engine']['rules'] if x['id'].startswith('OF590') and x['id'] not in {y['id'] for y in p['rule_engine']['rules']}]),clinical_use_authorised=False)
